.TH SDL_RunOnMainThread 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_RunOnMainThread \- Call a function on the main thread during event processing.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_init.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_RunOnMainThread(SDL_MainThreadCallback callback, void *userdata, bool wait_complete);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If this is called on the main thread, the callback is executed immediately\[char46] If this is called on another thread, this callback is queued for execution on the main thread during event processing\[char46]
.PP
Be careful of deadlocks when using this functionality\[char46] You should not have the main thread wait for the current thread while this function is being called with
.BR wait_complete
true\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I callback
the callback to call on the main thread\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
a pointer that is passed to
.BR callback \[char46]

.TP
.I wait_complete
true to wait for the callback to complete, false to return immediately\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_IsMainThread (3)
